    <innerclass refid="classLogger" prot="public">Logger</innerclass>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Drogon/Trantor logging bridged to an asynchronous spdlog logger. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Declares the <ref refid="classLogger" kindref="compound">Logger</ref> class, which owns one asynchronous spdlog logger and configures it at construction time. The logger can write to a rotating file, a coloured console, or both, based on the server configuration. Constructing it initialises spdlog&apos;s worker thread pool, registers the logger by name, makes it spdlog&apos;s default and installs it as Trantor&apos;s spdlog backend. The log() method forwards a Trantor record at the matching spdlog severity. A colour enum and several size/thread constants support the setup.</para>
<para>WHY THIS FILE MATTERS IN THE SERVER: This class is the single logging hub for the whole process. Framework messages from Drogon/Trantor, utility messages from <ref refid="classMessage" kindref="compound">Message</ref> and application messages all end up in the same sinks with the same format. It is meant to be created once as a process-wide singleton through <ref refid="classStore" kindref="compound">Store</ref>; spdlog registration is global, so two instances would clash. Without it there would be no unified, non-blocking log output for the server.</para>
<para>CONCEPTS TO LEARN (for beginners):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>std::shared_ptr: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/shared_ptr">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/shared_ptr</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>spdlog asynchronous logging: <ulink url="https://github.com/gabime/spdlog/wiki/5.-Asynchronous-logging">https://github.com/gabime/spdlog/wiki/5.-Asynchronous-logging</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>enum types: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/enum">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/enum</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>static constexpr members: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/static#Static_data_members">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/static#Static_data_members</ulink></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Amr Osman <ulink url="mailto:dr3mro@gmail.com">dr3mro@gmail.com</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2026-11-16 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
